[ti:The Face That Never Sleeps]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:1984s.text - Rectified]
[length:03:13.91]

[00:05.70]Bright cold April... the clocks are striking thirteen
[00:15.82]Attention, comrades... a bulletin from the Ministry of Plenty
[00:19.99]Production is up. Again
[00:22.36]The chocolate ration has been generously raised... to twenty grams
[00:26.72]Big Brother thanks you
[00:29.83]Last week it was thirty
[00:32.45]Six-zero-seven-nine, Smith W.! Yes, you. We can see you
[00:39.70]...It never sleeps
[00:51.11]Dust swirls through the doors of the concrete dream
[00:55.64]Posters on every wall, larger than life
[01:00.70]Heavy black gaze follows you through the night
[01:09.74]Telescreen whispers in the corner of the room
[01:11.82]Boiled cabbage air, Victory Gin perfume
[01:14.27]You turn your back but the eyes stay glued
[01:16.61]Every movement measured, every breath reviewed
[01:19.33]Victory Mansions, the lift is dead again
[01:24.12]Seven floors of stairs, the same face on each landing
[01:29.23]The face that never sleeps... always watching you
[01:34.01]Big Brother never blinks, nothing you can do
[01:38.84]He never looks away
[01:42.48]He reads you before your mouth can find the words
[01:53.20]Pipes burst in the frost, the gin burns on your tongue
[01:57.68]A helicopter snooping at a window, then it's gone
[02:02.28]Next door the children play at hanging spies
[02:04.65]Three slogans carved in elegant white
[02:07.34]War is peace... freedom is slavery
[02:12.20]Ignorance is strength
[02:14.84]The face that never sleeps... always watching you
[02:19.61]Big Brother never blinks, nothing you can do
[02:24.49]He never looks away
[02:27.45]You're already gone... you're already erased
[02:34.02]No escape in the dark, no escape in the light
[02:38.82]Every cubic centimetre of your skull is bright
[02:48.44]The face that never sleeps
[02:53.48]Thirteen... and the screen never says goodnight
[03:12.94]
